# Newton–Gauss line — the midpoints of the three diagonals of a complete quadrilateral are collinear (source: Newton/Gauss; Johnson, Advanced Euclidean Geometry)
A B C = triangle
D = free
E = meet(line(A, B), line(C, D))
F = meet(line(A, D), line(B, C))
M1 = midpoint(A, C)
M2 = midpoint(B, D)
M3 = midpoint(E, F)
prove coll(M1, M2, M3)
